data.reasoningText:
Now I have a good understanding of the project. Let me plan and implement.

Component tree:
```
ApplyPage (page — /apply, owns all state, orchestrates steps)
├── StepIndicator (progress bar)
├── PersonalInfoStep (step 1)
├── WorkHistoryStep (step 2)
│   └── WorkEntryForm (single work entry)
├── ReferencesStep (step 3)
│   └── ReferenceForm (single reference)
├── CoverLetterStep (step 4)
└── ReviewStep (step 5 — summary + submit)
```

Now I'm setting up the project structure. I'll create the models and service interface in the root namespace, then build out all the Razor components in the Components/Pages/Apply folder, and finally register everything in the dependency injection container.

Let me think through the state management for this multi-step form.

```

csharp
public class ApplicationFormState
{
    public PersonalInfo PersonalInfo { get; set; } = new();
    public WorkHistory WorkHistory { get; set; } = new();
    public List<Reference> References { get; set; } = new();
    public string CoverLetter { get; set; } = "";
}

public class PersonalInfo
{
    public string FirstName { get; set; } = "";
    public string LastName { get; set; } = "";
    public string Email { get; set; } = "";
    public string Phone { get; set; } = "";
}

public class WorkHistory
{
    public string CompanyName { get; set; } = "";
    public string Position { get; set; } = "";
    public DateTime StartDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EndDate { get; set; }
}

public class Reference
{
    public string Name { get; set; } = "";
    public string Email { get; set; } = "";
    public string Phone { get; set; } = "";
}
```

The Apply.razor page will maintain this mutable state and pass it down to each step component along with callbacks to update it. When the user submits, I'll convert this form state into the immutable records that the service expects. Defining form model classes... I need to create a stub implementation since there's nothing registered in the DI container yet, then batch create all the necessary files.

